    "circle_ios_fallback_text": "Exercise 11.1: Clean Up and Generate Your AI Master PromptPurposeIn this cohort, adding SOPs, guides, and blueprints to your project was intentional so Claude could learn your business deeply.Now the goal is to clean and consolidate that content so your Master Prompt is high quality, not repetitive, and easier to maintain.In this exercise, you will:- Resolve conflicting information across files- Remove duplicate or low-value repetition- Keep the important SOP/guide content that improves output quality- Generate a clean Master Prompt package you can activate in Stage 3Target: keep your active Master Prompt as lean as possible (ideally around 80k tokens), without removing important operating context.Time to complete: 30-60 minutes  Deadline: Before Session 12InstructionsStep 1: Open Claude in Your Company MP Project- Go to claude.ai- Open your Company Master Prompt project- Start a NEW chat- Confirm the project name appears at the topStep 2: Run the Session 11.1 PromptCopy and paste the Session 11.1 prompt:Claude will guide you one question at a time and help you:- Find and resolve conflicts- Remove redundancy- Keep the right level of SOP/guide detail- Produce final artifacts ready for Stage 3Step 3: Review the Artifacts Claude ProducesBy the end, you should have:1. Cleaned AI Master Prompt Source2. Cleanup Change Log3. Optional Supporting Reference Pack (only if Claude identifies content that should be reference-only)Quick review checklist:- Core strategy, operating rules, and SOP intelligence are preserved- Duplicate sections are removed- Conflicts are resolved and documented- Final content is clean enough to activateNext Steps After Exercise 11.1Step 1: Add to Stage 3 (AI Master Prompts)1. Go to Stage 3 > AI Master Prompts2. Create a New Master Prompt (top right button) and then click “Add Document” and add the cleaned file(s) Claude generated3. Enable the file(s) you want included in your active AI Master Prompt4. Click Generate Master Prompt, and click Set as Default.Step 2: Create a new project in Claude",
